# Build output must never enter the image context. Copying a host obj/ directory over the container's
# restore output makes `dotnet publish --no-restore` read a project.assets.json full of host paths,
# which fails the build in a way whose error message does not mention the cause.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Test projects are not part of the published image. Root-level on purpose: the dashboard's own
# tests/ directory is part of its build, because `pnpm build` type-checks it.
tests/
benchmarks/

# A pattern without a leading **/ matches at the root of the context only, so these are anchored at
# every depth. The dashboard stage copies web/AgentSplice.Dashboard/: a host node_modules there would
# overwrite the one the stage installed — with the host's native binaries, which fail the build from
# a Windows checkout — and a host dist would be stale output. A host *.db under src/ is a development
# store holding trace metadata, which has no business in an image's build context.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/TestResults/
artifacts/

.env
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
/data/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
